        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Accessions register entry: 'Robe of a chief. Blue cotton, worked in coloured silks round the neck amd down the front and back with an angular pattern and corded spirals; it is further decorated with holes cut and sewn round with silk. From the Gambia River. / African. L. 4ft. W. 5ft 4 1/2in. / 21 Oct 1875 / Given by Mrs Foy, 28 Aden Grove, North. See R.P. 3441/1875, 3245/1875.'"@en ;
